ht displays the text \\\"30 Oral Thin Strips\\\" next to a small, white peeled-strip icon. Centered in the blue upper section is a graphic of a white crescent moon partially behind a dark blue cloud, accented by small white stars. Below this, the product name \\\"melts® into a restful sleep\\\" is printed in white, with the words \\\"restful\\\" and \\\"sleep\\\" encased in two separate, dark-blue rectangular blocks. The lower white section displays the blue text \\\"Melatonin - 10mg\\\" above a short black-text product description, followed by \\\"Lemon Honey Flavour\\\" next to a small yellow and blue lemon icon, \\\"NUTRACEUTICAL FOR ADULTS\\\" in small black capitals at the bottom left, and a small green square vegetarian symbol at the bottom right. A circular silver \\\"Advanced Molecular Science\\\" seal with a stylized atom graphic sits along the right edge of the container, bridging the blue-and-white color transition. The corresponding oral thin strip is a flexible, semi-translucent, rectangular film with a uniform caramel-brown hue, slightly rounded corners, and a matte texture.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"status\":\"generating\",\"createdBy\":\"f5dfb377-dac7-46a6-aea3-a4e04cb45e54\",\"metadata\":{\"brief\":\"Using the Feature-Benefit-Action (FBA) framework, this ad appeals to routine-builders looking to optimize their wind-down ritual with a clean-label solution. The visual hero is the aspirational bedroom nightstand setup, showcasing the product integrated into a peaceful evening routine. Set against a soft Wellness Cream (#fff9eb) background, the image features a beautifully lit, warm lifestyle shot of a modern nightstand holding a ceramic mug of tea and the pocket-sized blue-and-white Melts packaging next to a single, matte-textured caramel-brown strip. The on-image headline is \\\"Your 10-Second Nightly Sleep Ritual.\\\" Below this, a clean, low-text layout highlights the fast-acting, lemon-honey-flavored 10mg Melatonin benefit, paired with an urgent \\\"Buy 2, Get 1 Free - Sale Ends Tonight\\\" bundle offer to compel immediate purchase. The CTA is a high-impact, sharp-cornered button utilizing the Action Gradient (#ff9000 to #ff5000) that reads \\\"Claim Free Pack\\\". Ensure brand alignment by pairing Tenor Sans for the elegant headline with Outfit for the clean supporting text, keeping the photographic style bright, comforting, and organic.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the Feature-Benefit-Action (FBA) framework, this ad appeals to routine-builders looking to optimize their wind-down ritual with a clean-label solution. The visual hero is the aspirational bedroom nightsta